{
  "id": "documention-documention",
  "slug": "documention",
  "title": "Documention",
  "category": "Spring Framework",
  "sections": [
    {
      "id": "what-is-rest-api-documentation",
      "heading": "What is REST API Documentation?",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Definition:"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "REST API documentation is the process of describing how a client can interact with a RESTful API. This includes:"
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "ordered": false,
          "items": [
            "Endpoint URLs",
            "Supported HTTP methods (GET, POST, PUT, DELETE)",
            "Request and response formats",
            "Required parameters and their types",
            "Response codes",
            "Return data format (e.g., JSON, XML)"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Purpose:"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "To enable developers to understand and use your API correctly, efficiently, and securely."
        }
      ],
      "wordCount": 60,
      "subsections": []
    },
    {
      "id": "traditional-sharing-methods-drawbacks",
      "heading": "Traditional Sharing Methods – Drawbacks",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "APIs can be documented and shared via:"
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "ordered": false,
          "items": [
            "Emails",
            "Documents (PDF, Word)",
            "Spreadsheets",
            "Messaging apps"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Issue: These methods lack real-time updates. Any changes in the API (e.g., new endpoints, removed parameters) can quickly become outdated, leading to confusion and integration failures."
        }
      ],
      "wordCount": 40,
      "subsections": []
    },
    {
      "id": "api-documentation-tools-solution",
      "heading": "API Documentation Tools – Solution",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Definition:"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "An API documentation tool generates real-time, interactive documentation for APIs. It automatically syncs with the API source code and updates when the API changes."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Benefits:"
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "ordered": false,
          "items": [
            "Always up-to-date documentation",
            "Accessible via web interface",
            "Easier sharing across teams",
            "Often includes testing functionality"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "wordCount": 41,
      "subsections": []
    },
    {
      "id": "wadl-web-application-description-language",
      "heading": "WADL (Web Application Description Language)",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Definition:"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "WADL is an XML-based format for describing RESTful web services."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Key Features:"
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "ordered": false,
          "items": [
            "Machine-readable",
            "Describes resources and how they relate",
            "Can auto-generate client stubs in Java"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Limitation:"
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "ordered": false,
          "items": [
            "XML format is not human-friendly",
            "Rarely used now in favor of OpenAPI/Swagger"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "src": "/Users/luffy/Desktop/Computer Science/Infosys/Spring Rest/Documention/Documention/image.png",
          "alt": "image.png",
          "originalPath": "Documention/image.png"
        }
      ],
      "wordCount": 39,
      "subsections": []
    },
    {
      "id": "openapi-specification-oas",
      "heading": "OpenAPI Specification (OAS)",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Definition:"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "OpenAPI is a language-agnostic standard for describing REST APIs in a format that is both human- and machine-readable."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Features:"
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "ordered": false,
          "items": [
            "Standardized format (typically YAML or JSON)",
            "Can describe endpoints, parameters, response schemas, authentication, etc.",
            "Tooling support: code generation, validation, interactive docs"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Widely adopted by: Google, Microsoft, IBM, and other tech companies."
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "src": "/Users/luffy/Desktop/Computer Science/Infosys/Spring Rest/Documention/Documention/image%201.png",
          "alt": "image.png",
          "originalPath": "Documention/image%201.png"
        }
      ],
      "wordCount": 51,
      "subsections": []
    },
    {
      "id": "swagger-implementation-of-openapi",
      "heading": "Swagger – Implementation of OpenAPI",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Definition:"
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "ordered": false,
          "items": [
            "Swagger is a popular open-source toolkit for working with the OpenAPI specification."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Capabilities:"
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "ordered": false,
          "items": [
            "Design and build APIs",
            "Generate interactive documentation",
            "Provide live testing UI",
            "Generate server/client code in various languages"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "src": "/Users/luffy/Desktop/Computer Science/Infosys/Spring Rest/Documention/Documention/b115a045-d1f1-4112-be86-1e3adc76348c.png",
          "alt": "image.png",
          "originalPath": "Documention/b115a045-d1f1-4112-be86-1e3adc76348c.png"
        }
      ],
      "wordCount": 31,
      "subsections": [
        {
          "id": "step-1-add-dependency",
          "heading": "Step 1: Add Dependency",
          "level": 3,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "In your Spring Boot application's pom.xml:"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "language": "xml",
              "code": "<dependency>\n    <groupId>org.springdoc</groupId>\n    <artifactId>springdoc-openapi-ui</artifactId>\n    <version>1.6.14</version> <!-- or latest version -->\n</dependency>",
              "runnable": false
            }
          ],
          "wordCount": 6,
          "subsections": []
        },
        {
          "id": "step-2-access-documentation",
          "heading": "Step 2: Access Documentation",
          "level": 3,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Once your application is running, access:"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "language": "",
              "code": "http://localhost:8080/swagger-ui.html",
              "runnable": false
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "or"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "language": "",
              "code": "http://localhost:8080/swagger-ui/index.html",
              "runnable": false
            }
          ],
          "wordCount": 7,
          "subsections": []
        },
        {
          "id": "step-3-use-openapi-annotations-for-customization",
          "heading": "Step 3: Use OpenAPI Annotations for Customization",
          "level": 3,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Example:"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "language": "java",
              "code": "@OpenAPIDefinition(\n  info = @Info(title = \"Customer API\", version = \"1.0\", description = \"API for customer operations\")\n)\n@RestController\npublic class CustomerController {\n\n    @Operation(summary = \"Get customer by ID\")\n    @ApiResponse(responseCode = \"200\", description = \"Success\")\n    @GetMapping(\"/customers/{id}\")\n    public Customer getCustomer(@PathVariable String id) {\n        // method implementation\n    }\n}",
              "runnable": false
            }
          ],
          "wordCount": 1,
          "subsections": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "built-in-api-testing-with-swagger",
      "heading": "Built-in API Testing with Swagger",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Swagger includes a live API testing tool, where users can:"
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "ordered": false,
          "items": [
            "Select endpoints",
            "Enter parameters and request body",
            "Execute HTTP requests directly from the browser",
            "View real-time responses"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "💡 This removes the need for tools like Postman or SoapUI during development!"
        }
      ],
      "wordCount": 40,
      "subsections": []
    },
    {
      "id": "summary",
      "heading": "Summary",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Feature",
            "WADL",
            "OpenAPI / Swagger"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Format",
              "XML",
              "YAML / JSON"
